mammoth 1.12.0

Vendored from node_modules/mammoth by the Cloudflare port (P4). One file,
copied verbatim:

  mammoth.browser.min.js  ->  mammoth.browser.min.js

WHY IT IS HERE. PORT-CLOUDFLARE.md §6: a Worker on the free plan gets ~10 ms of
CPU per request, and converting a chapter-length .docx is nowhere near that. So
the conversion runs in the UPLOADER'S BROWSER — public/js/upload-cf.js loads
this file on demand (only for a .docx submit) and posts the resulting pages back
to be sanitized and stored. The Express app on `main` still uses the Node build
of the same library and the same version, so a document converts identically on
either stack.

It is a UMD bundle and publishes `window.mammoth`. It is loaded from this origin
because the Content-Security-Policy in worker/src/index.js and src/app.js is
`script-src 'self'` — nothing is ever fetched from a CDN.

To upgrade: bump mammoth in package.json, re-copy the file, rewrite the version
line above, and re-run an upload of the .docx fixture end to end.
